o a thin-provisioned volume by using volume mirroring:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":684.3333333333334,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":135.33333333333334,"r":544.3333333333334,"t":723.3333333333334},"charspan":[0,245],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"thin-provisioned volume feature that is called zero detect provides clients with the ability to reclaim unused allocated disk space (zeros) when they are converting a fully allocated volume to a thin-provisioned volume by using volume mirroring:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3.12 Host attachment planning","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":640.3333333333334,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":63.333333333333336,"r":303.6666666666667,"t":662.3333333333334},"charspan":[0,29],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"3.12 Host attachment planning"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The typical FC host attachment to the Storwize V7OOO is done through SAN fabric. However, the system allows direct attachment connectivity between its 8 Gb or 16 Gb Fibre Channel ports and host ports. No configuration is required for host systems that are this configuration. However, the maximum number of directly attached hosts is severely limited by the number of FC ports on Storwize V7OOO's nodes. special using","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":567.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":135.0,"r":546.3333333333334,"t":628.3333333333334},"charspan":[0,417],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"The typical FC host attachment to the Storwize V7OOO is done through SAN fabric. However, the system allows direct attachment connectivity between its 8 Gb or 16 Gb Fibre Channel ports and host ports. No configuration is required for host systems that are this configuration. However, the maximum number of directly attached hosts is severely limited by the number of FC ports on Storwize V7OOO's nodes. special using"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The Storwize V7OOO imposes no particular limit on the distance between the Storwize V70OO nodes and host servers. However, for host attachment; the Storwize V7OOO supports up to three ISL hops in the fabric. This capacity means that the server to the Storwize V7OOO can be separated by up to five FC links; four of which can be 10 km long (6.2 miles) if long wave Small Form-factor Pluggables (SFPs) are used.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":497.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":135.0,"r":546.6666666666666,"t":559.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,409],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"The Storwize V7OOO imposes no particular limit on the distance between the Storwize V70OO nodes and host servers. However, for host attachment; the Storwize V7OOO supports up to three ISL hops in the fabric. This capacity means that the server to the Storwize V7OOO can be separated by up to five FC links; four of which can be 10 km long (6.2 miles) if long wave Small Form-factor Pluggables (SFPs) are used."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Figure 3-9 shows an example of a supported configuration with Storwize V7OOO nodes using shortwave SFPs","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":465.3333333333333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":135.0,"r":547.0,"t":490.0},"charspan":[0,103],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"Figure 3-9 shows an example of a supported configuration with Storwize V7OOO nodes using shortwave SFPs"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Figure 3-9 Example of host connectivity","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":205.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.33333333333334,"r":301.6666666666667,"t":218.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,39],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"Figure 3-9 Example of host connectivity"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Host","parent":{"$ref":"#/